{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIxL0NyZWF0aW9uJTIwU3RvcmllcyUyMCUyODIwMjElMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Creation Stories","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/2qjWOHYUjJhw5qe86Qk790vaegf.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/alITbloN2ALx18YGHLzCoUP2st3.jpg","description":"The true story of the rise and fall of Creation Records and its infamous founder Alan McGee; the man responsible for supplying the “Brit Pop” soundtrack to the ‘90s, a decade of cultural renaissance known as Cool Britannia.  From humble beginnings to Downing Street soirées, from dodging bailiffs to releasing multi-platinum albums, Creation had it all. Breakdowns, bankruptcy, fights and friendships… and not forgetting the music. Featuring some of the greatest records you have ever heard, we follow Alan through a drug-fuelled haze of music and mayhem, as his rock’n’roll dream brings the world Oasis, Primal Scream, and other generation-defining bands.\n\nRated 18 · Released 15 Apr 2021 · United Kingdom, United States of America · Language: English · 110 min\nStudio: Burning Wheel Productions, Head Gear Films, Metrol Technology\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2021","genres":["Drama","Music","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.9","runtime":"110 min","cast":["Ewen Bremner","Suki Waterhouse","Richard Jobson","Seána Kerslake","Leo Flanagan","Charlie Murphy","Jason Flemyng","Jason Isaacs"],"director":["Nick Moran"],"released":"2021-04-15T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"One man created a soundtrack that defined a generation.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Nick Moran","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kfWebCAm72JBZLXcNbA2Myr950E.jpg"},{"name":"Ewen Bremner","character":"Alan McGee","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7ZayRqxxy5JsQpiUPA0iVeRHny6.jpg"},{"name":"Suki Waterhouse","character":"Gemma","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/bpGRoG2DRsySQBICMzCuvfFDg0e.jpg"},{"name